<step1>
<ptxt>Checking Malfunction Occurrence Conditions Using Freeze Frame Data</ptxt>
<step2>
<ptxt>Freeze Frame Data When Malfunction DTC Occurs</ptxt>
<step3>
<ptxt>If freeze frame data from when a malfunction DTC occurred is stored, "F" is displayed for the relevant DTC on the DTC display screen.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>When freeze frame data from when a malfunction code occurred is stored, the previously stored freeze frame data from system operation is cleared.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Once freeze frame data from when a malfunction code occurred is stored, the data is not updated until the stored data is cleared (DTCs cleared).</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</step3>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>Freeze Frame Data During System Operation</ptxt>
<step3>
<ptxt>Freeze frame data during system operation is updated with new data each time the system operates.</ptxt>
</step3>
<step3>
<ptxt>The number of times the IG has been turned OFF → ON since the system last operated is stored and displayed up to 31 times.</ptxt>
</step3>
<step3>
<ptxt>Using the number of IG ON times since the data freeze, you can check whether the displayed data is from when the malfunction pointed out by the customer occurred, using the following formula as a guide. ("Number of IG ON times per 1 day" × "Number of days since the malfunction occurred" = "Number of IG ON times since data freeze")</ptxt>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Turning the IG OFF → ON while the vehicle is stopped (vehicle speed 7km/h or less) is not counted.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If the number of IG ON times since the data freeze exceeds 31, "31" is displayed.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</step3>
</step2>
</step1>
